# Trivy ignore file for Terraform security scanning
# This file tells Trivy which security issues to ignore during scanning

# Common Terraform false positives that are acceptable for this project
# Add specific CVE IDs or rule IDs here if needed

# CloudFront Origin Access Control (OAC) requires these settings to be disabled
# for static website hosting buckets to work properly with CloudFront
AVD-AWS-0087  # Public access block does not block public policies - Required for CloudFront OAC
AVD-AWS-0093  # Public access block does not restrict public buckets - Required for CloudFront OAC

# ECR mutable tags are required for container layer building
# We need to overwrite the 'latest' tag during development/deployment
# This is acceptable for our use case as the container only runs during deployment
AVD-AWS-0031  # Repository tags are mutable - Required for container layer building

# Example of ignoring specific issues:
# AVD-AWS-0001
# CVE-2021-12345

# For now, this file is empty but prevents the "ignorefile not found" error
